# Token efficiency

## Before asking the agent
- One task per message. Name the file or folder when you know it (`apps/web/...`, `apps/api/...`, `apps/mobile/...`).
- Prefer `@folder` or `@file` over `@Codebase` unless the location is unknown.
- Paste only the failing log lines (10–30 lines), not full CI output. Link GitHub Actions runs instead.
- For “is CI green?”, link the run URL; don’t paste job logs unless something failed.

## Scope
- Web/API/mobile are separate dependency trees. Don’t touch `apps/mobile` when fixing web CI, and vice versa.
- Docs-only or mobile-only changes should not trigger full deploy discussion unless deploy is the ask.
- Minimize diff scope: fix the root cause, don’t refactor adjacent code.

## Exploration
- Search/grep before reading whole files. Read only the function or component in scope.
- Don’t re-run full E2E locally unless the change touches UI journeys or Playwright config.
- Don’t regenerate lockfiles unless dependency graphs actually changed; always verify with `npm ci` from a clean tree.

## Long tasks
- Use Plan mode for architecture or multi-file design; switch to Agent for the implementation.
- Split large work into reviewable chunks (web, API, mobile, infra) instead of one mega-prompt.
- Prefer `workflow_dispatch` or path-filtered CI when validating unrelated areas.

## Models
- Default/fast models for lint fixes, config tweaks, and small diffs.
- Stronger models for RAG/AI logic, cross-app refactors, or ambiguous production failures.
